    She goes to college right by my house, and she lives there. There&apos;s a guy that works there, name is unimportant. So things were going pretty good for a few months, then a friendship develops between her and this guy. Nothing too out of the ordinary, and he was a pretty cool guy, and it turned into a mutual friendship for all of us.

    Few months after we started talking to this guy, he texts her asking if she was single would they hook up, etc. And this is right at the time we&apos;re having more problems. She tells me we need to take a break, and we can hook up with others during the break. I didn&apos;t, because I knew the shitstorm that would ensue, and I&apos;m a halfway decent guy, so I didn&apos;t want/need to. She is different. Less than 24 hours after, she fucks him. She tells me about her crush on him, and how attracted she is to him, etc. We end up getting back together, and neither of us talk to him anymore. As far as I know, she doesn&apos;t even know what she saw in him.

    But after all of this, I&apos;m left feeling like the problems that occurred in this relationship would be too much for me to overlook. The way she acts, how she responds to stress, everything. I love her so much, but I&apos;m still feeling like this relationship is basically over, and the longer we stay with each other, the more harmful it is to both of us.

